WEBVTT

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.960
E-Excuse me!

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.910
I hate to trouble you when you're busy, but...

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.120
Could you read my fortune?

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.110
In particular, about romance?

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.600
Will my love be realized?

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:54.190
Your love...

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.610
will never be realized.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:40.820
<b>Fukada 
Ryuusuke</b>

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:39.200
Let me introduce your new classmate,

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.520
Fukada Ryuusuke-kun.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:44.660
Fukada-kun used to live here in town,

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.090
so some of you might remember him.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.820
Hey, do you remember me?

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:57.490
I went to kindergarten with you!

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.800
Wait, are you Midori-chan?

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:01.920
Yeah!

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.450
You actually remembered!

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.890
Ryuusuke-kun, let me introduce 
you to my best friend.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.970
This is Tanaka Suzue-san from Class B.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.280
It's nice to meet you.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.540
Likewise.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.720
The girls in our class were all 
talking about you, Ryuusuke-san.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.500
They think you're cute.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:24.410
But none of them think they have
a chance because of Midori-san.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.920
Come on, Suzue-chan,
what are you saying?

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.150
Y'know, Ryuusuke-san,

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:30.830
Midori-chan is really popular
with the boys at our school.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.940
She's the target of all the guys' affections!

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.650
Or maybe more like the 
target of their fortunes?

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.990
Guys practically clog the streets

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:41.620
trying to get their compatibility 
with her read. Right, Midori-chan?

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.530
Jeez, cut it out before Ryuusuke-kun
starts taking you seriously.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:48.070
Besides, it's not like crossroads
fortune-telling could ever be real.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:49.560
That stuff's a waste of time.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.560
Oh, I wouldn't say that.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:56.540
Do you really think some random passerby
would have any kind of special insight?

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.610
True enough, but still...

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:00.970
What do you think, Ryuusuke-san?

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.720
You know about crossroads
fortune-telling, right?

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.130
You shouldn't mess with that stuff.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.600
<i>On a day like this,</i>

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:22.700
<i>I bet tons of people stand on crossroads 
at dusk, wanting their fortune told.</i>

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:26.230
<i>And I bet every one of them
asks something like this:</i>

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:30.370
<i>"Will my love be realized?"</i>

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:35.700
I heard a first-year girl died yesterday.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:40.240
She was in the middle of an intersection,
her neck sliced open by a box cutter...

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.340
It was practically an ocean of blood.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:45.120
Why would she kill herself?

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.290
I don't know.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:50.120
There was no note, and the fog was 
so thick, there were no witnesses.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:53.210
Some people think she wanted
a crossroads fortune, though.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.310
How would they know?

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:58.730
There was apparently a case just 
like this, seven or eight years ago.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:02.600
A girl who was trying to get her fortune
told at the crossroads committed suicide.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.370
Really?

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.100
That's scary.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.920
<i>How did I end up back in this town?</i>

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:16.530
<i>It must be punishment.</i>

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.610
<i>I'm being punished!</i>

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:20.340
Little boy...

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.000
Little boy.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:25.090
Little boy...

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:27.710
Please, could you come here?

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.260
Will you hear me out?

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.140
And then tell me...

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.440
See, there's someone I love right now.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.600
I love him very much.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:42.520
But he has a wife, and a child.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:43.910
But you see,

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:47.990
another one of his babies
is inside me, too.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.580
Do you understand?

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.000
I want to have his baby, too.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.170
But he suddenly started acting cold, 
and says I should get rid of it.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:57.420
Isn't that mean?

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:59.900
But I still like him...

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.030
I love him!

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:02.450
I'm in love with him!

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:06.400
Yes, I'm so deeply in love 
with him that I could die!

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:09.420
So, what should I do, little boy?

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.430
I don't get what you're saying!

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:14.310
What I'm asking, little boy, is...

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:17.690
Will my love with him be realized?

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.390
Or won't it?

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:22.230
Of course it won't, stupid!

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:34.370
<i>But that night,</i>

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.820
<i>I got curious about that woman.</i>

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:40.480
<i>I wondered what had happened to her.</i>

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:45.290
<i>So I went to the same spot the next day.</i>

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.810
<i>I was the one who killed her.</i>

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.360
<i>It's my fault she and her unborn baby are...</i>

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:01.700
Ryuusuke-kun?

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.210
What's wrong?

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:05.620
You seem kind of down.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.020
Midori-chan?

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.900
You've been acting weird lately.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.620
Is something bothering you?

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.900
No, it's nothing.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.780
If you say so...

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.750
Y'know...

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.840
I was wondering if you had

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:23.430
a bad experience with a
crossroads fortune or something.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:25.610
C'mon, you're overthinking this.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:27.090
You're so weird.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:32.210
I mean, I have bad memories
tied to them myself.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:36.130
You heard the girls talking
about it in class, right?

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:39.970
About the woman who killed
herself eight years ago...

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:43.480
That was actually my aunt.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.200
It can't be...

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.900
This can't be!

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.200
Midori-chan!

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:00.820
Suzue-chan.

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:02.740
Walking home alone again?

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:03.330
Yeah.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.110
What's wrong?

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:07.800
Are things going badly with Ryuusuke-san?

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.800
Actually, yeah...

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.420
I think he's been avoiding me lately...

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.250
And I have no idea why.

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:17.880
I can ask him for you.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:19.970
There's bound to be a reason behind it.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:23.440
Why are you avoiding Midori-chan?

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:26.010
Did she do something to upset you?

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.890
Ryuusuke-san?

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.070
I could never be upset with her.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:35.330
But I don't deserve to like her!

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:37.040
Or even talk to her!

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:39.010
It's all my fault!

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:40.830
So I can't help it...

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:44.700
What are you talking about, Ryuusuke-san?

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.090
This isn't normal.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:47.700
Tell me what's going on.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:50.180
I'm sure I can help somehow!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.880
What happened, Ryuusuke-san?

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:53.840
That's enough!

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:56.020
Don't ask me anything else!

00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:00.270
She'll suffer less if we just let it end now.

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:04.110
But Midori-chan is worried 
about what's going on...

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.020
But... all right. I'll let it go.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:09.020
Sorry for calling you out like this.

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:10.720
Goodbye.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.660
Oh, I know.

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:42.850
U-Um... Excuse me!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.760
I was hoping to get a
crossroads fortune told.

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:47.400
Will you help me?

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.590
It's... about a friend of mine.

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:54.930
She's been troubled by how distant
her boyfriend's been lately,

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:58.480
and he also seems to be 
troubled by something...

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:02.370
What do you think I should do to get 
them back together, like before?

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:11.760
You should be more worried
about your own love life.

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:17.050
Hey, Suzue-chan.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:19.700
Did Ryuusuke-kun say anything?

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:20.700
Yeah...

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.170
I asked him,

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:24.990
and he says he wants
to break it off with you.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:25.980
I see...

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:30.730
I tried getting a crossroads fortune 
about the two of you.

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:33.600
About whether or not you
could get back together.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:36.310
You did all that, Suzue-chan?

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:37.840
Yeah, I did.

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:42.000
I think I ran into the "crossroads
pretty boy" that people talk about.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.450
He was the first person to 
walk by at the intersection!

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:47.240
He was really tall,

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:48.720
wore all black,

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:50.880
and had a sharp look on his face...

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.590
He had this cold beauty
that gave me the chills.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:57.100
But more than that, more than anything,

00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:00.560
what shook me the most is what he said...

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:05.300
It made me realize I was lying to myself.

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.310
That I was doing the opposite
of what I really wanted.

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:12.000
I'm going to live more
honestly from now on.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.340
So, Midori-chan, I'm going
to come out and tell you...

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.770
I like Ryuusuke-san!

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.900
Ever since he transferred in.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.610
I'm sorry, Midori-chan,

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.990
but I love Ryuusuke-san.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.340
So much I could die!

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:29.650
So I'm actually really lucky
the two of you are splitting up!

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:30.610
Goodbye.

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:33.190
I'm gonna go tell
Ryuusuke-san how I feel!

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:39.220
<i>Tanaka Suzue has started
aggressively pursuing me.</i>

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:43.500
<i>But my attempts to gently turn
her down didn't seem to work.</i>

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:46.700
<i>If anything, she started to 
act even more bizarrely.</i>

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:49.100
Here's your lunch.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.400
Can you cut this out already?

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:54.060
If you keep following me around,
I'm gonna call the police!

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:58.020
But... you needed lunch today...

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.050
I have lunch!

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:01.890
Then eat mine instead!

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:04.720
I'll get rid of the one in your bag!

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:06.740
What are you doing?! Stop it!

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:10.130
Would you just stop already?!

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:11.470
I'm going to be blunt.

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:13.540
I don't like you!

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.220
I like Midori!

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:17.140
I have no place in my life for you!

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:18.300
So get lost!

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:19.350
No...

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:21.920
But what will become of my love?!

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:22.880
I don't care!

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:26.070
But I did just as the crossroads fortune said...

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:28.480
The pretty boy who showed
up at the crossroads

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.640
told me to worry about my own love life,

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.890
so I did just that.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.890
And yet... And yet...

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:38.100
My love isn't going to be realized?

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:40.860
I love you, Ryuusuke-san.

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:44.110
I love you! So much I could die!

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:51.410
I heard there was another
suicide at an intersection.

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:54.120
That makes four...

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.580
Apparently she was having her fortune told.

00:12:56.310 --> 00:13:01.800
And I heard she ran into the 
crossroads pretty boy, too.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.470
Maybe he's the angel of death.

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:07.190
The pretty boy of the crossroads...

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:08.420
The angel of death...

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:09.730
Yeah.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:11.680
Speaking of,

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.400
there's someone pretty grim
with her eyes on you, too.

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:41.700
Suzue-chan, I went too far this morning.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:44.290
It's not that I dislike you.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:47.780
But I just can't forget about Midori-chan...

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:50.400
So I can't go out with someone else.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:59.110
I should have told you why I was 
avoiding Midori back when you asked.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:03.090
Eight years ago,

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:05.800
when I first lived in this town...

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.700
On that day...

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:16.620
Suzue-chan!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:22.100
<i>The pretty boy of the crossroads...</i>

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:26.630
<i>I can't just sit here and do nothing.</i>

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:30.720
<i>I have to find him...</i>

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:33.700
<i>And the first step is to tell someone
at the crossroads their fortune.</i>

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:38.910
<i>I'll give people who want their
fortunes read some hope.</i>

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:41.920
<i>I'll do the opposite of what he's doing.</i>

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:46.000
<i>Maybe that's the only way I can
counteract what he's doing.</i>

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:51.350
<i>I did everything I could to 
respond to people sincerely.</i>

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.710
<i>It may have been</i>

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:58.800
<i>because of the guilt I still felt about driving
that woman to suicide, eight years ago.</i>

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:02.120
<i>But eventually...</i>

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.220
Oh, hey, do you want your fortune told?

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:17.970
What... happened to you?

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:23.690
Excuse me... will my love... be realized?

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:25.640
I-It will!

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:27.110
I'm sure it will!

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:28.700
<i>This can't be...</i>

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:31.100
<i>But there's no doubt...</i>

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:34.520
<i>These are the girls who killed
themselves at the crossroads!</i>

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.500
<i>And the proof of that...</i>

00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:42.340
I love you!

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:44.250
I love you so much I could die!

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:51.010
<i>But I couldn't let myself
stop telling fortunes.</i>

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:53.430
Ryuusuke-kun?

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:56.220
Midori-chan?

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.710
Are you going to walk
around town again today?

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:03.190
I know you walk around to help people trying 
to get their fortunes told at crossroads.

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:06.210
Almost as if you're possessed.

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:08.580
Could you tell me why?

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.820
Why go so far?

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:12.400
I...

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:16.620
I can't stop until I catch
the crossroads pretty boy.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:18.160
No!

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.390
Ryuusuke-kun, don't go!

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:21.580
Ryuusuke-kun!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:34.970
<i>That's him!</i>

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.290
Hold it!

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:39.750
Stop!

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:48.810
Damn it!

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:50.030
I lost him!

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:52.570
I wonder where I am...

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:58.990
<i>This is...</i>

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:02.030
<i>It's the intersection from eight years ago!</i>

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:04.200
<i>I ended up here somehow!</i>

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:15.500
You're...

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:18.690
I...

00:17:30.810 --> 00:17:32.160
Ryuusuke-kun?

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:33.570
Ryuusuke-kun!

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:34.830
It's no use...

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:36.840
I can't tell where I am at all.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.250
<i>That's...</i>

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:52.510
<i>the crossroads pretty boy!</i>

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:55.680
<i>No, I...</i>

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:58.640
<i>I'm not here to get my fortune told!</i>

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:00.090
<i>I'm not.</i>

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:02.630
<i>I'm not...</i>

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:04.470
I'm not!

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:08.580
Ryuusuke-kun?

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:10.300
What are you doing here?

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:13.460
Someone pointed me in this direction.

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:15.400
What are you doing here?

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.730
I saw him!

00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:19.830
I saw the crossroads pretty boy!

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:20.890
What?!

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:22.190
Look!

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:28.900
<i>But the crossroads pretty boy
was nowhere to be found,</i>

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:31.260
<i>and the fog that had been so thick</i>

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:32.790
<i>vanished in the blink of an eye.</i>

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:37.800
Collection No. 080

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:37.800
<b>The Crossroads Pretty Boy
The Lovesick Dead</b>

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:42.100
<i>My friend Yuuko was
famous for being chatty,</i>

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.600
<i>but lately she barely says a thing.</i>

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:46.140
<i>Even when she does talk...</i>

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:48.300
Wehl...

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:51.790
Ladely I haff trouble tawking.

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:54.690
Yuuko, are you sure you're
not sick or something?

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:59.660
Buh I don' feel sick at awl...

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:01.140
<i>And now,</i>

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:04.710
<i>she's stopped coming to class.</i>

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:10.330
<b>Slug Girl</b>

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:10.330
Collection No. 066

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:16.000
Maybe she's out?

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:19.490
Huh?

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:31.590
We keep killing them,
but they keep oozing up!

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:34.450
It's because there's been no sunlight 
and it's so humid lately.

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:36.340
Give me some of that salt, will you?

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:38.570
Oh, Rie-chan!

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:40.370
It's been so long.

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:41.460
Hello.

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:43.730
You're here to check up on Yuuko, right?

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:45.030
She's in her room.

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:48.900
Yuuko, Rie-chan's here to see you!

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:49.740
Yuuko?

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:55.220
Yuuko...

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:57.510
Is something wrong inside your mouth?

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.130
Juh leeb me alohn!

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:03.090
Yuuko...

00:20:04.620 --> 00:20:06.310
What's wrong, Yuuko?

00:20:16.760 --> 00:20:17.770
Yuuko?!

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:28.720
Pleeh hehlp meh!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.600
I guess we have no choice...

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:33.080
What'll we do, dear?

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:37.040
Let's fill the bathtub with 
salt and put Yuuko in it.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:39.000
<b>Salt</b>

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:42.160
There.

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:44.720
That should do it. Now, Yuuko, get in.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:46.300
I know you can do it.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.990
You've got to open your mouth
wide once you get in, okay?

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:01.010
Dear, I know we need to do this,
but hasn't she been in too long?

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:03.010
Yuuko? You all right?

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:03.890
Oh, no!

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:05.820
I think she's fainted in there!

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:10.160
Wait, these are just Yuuko's pajamas!

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:11.780
Where'd she go?!

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:13.200
Yuuko?!

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:14.540
Where are you, Yuuko?!

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:15.800
What's this?

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:23.200
Where did her body go?!

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:24.450
Dear, look!

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:26.930
There's a tiny body at 
the base of her neck!

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:29.560
The salt made her shrink!

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:46.110
<i>Apparently, it still lives in their garden.</i>

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:50.290
<i>Like a snail, carrying a shell around...</i>

00:21:50.570 --> 00:21:54.040
<i>But apparently it's slimy in 
a way that's unique to slugs.</i>

00:21:54.610 --> 00:21:57.700
<i>And they say whenever
anyone gets close,</i>

00:21:57.700 --> 00:22:00.040
<i>the shell will stare in their direction,</i>

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:03.290
<i>with a sad look in its eyes.</i>

00:23:34.760 --> 00:23:39.730
Collection
